- During this project, I gained practical experience in setting up and working with a controlled cybersecurity laboratory environment.

- I learned how to use Kali Linux as an attacker/security testing machine and DVWA (Damn Vulnerable Web Application) as a deliberately vulnerable target. The lab helped me understand how different cybersecurity tools can be used together for network and web application security analysis.

## Network Configuration

- I learned how to configure virtual machines using NAT and Host-Only network adapters. The Host-Only network allowed Kali Linux and DVWA to communicate within an isolated environment.

- I also used the ping utility to verify connectivity between the attacker and target systems.

## Nmap

- I used Nmap to perform basic network reconnaissance and service enumeration.

- The command used in the project was:

            nmap -sV <DVWA-IP>

- Through the scan, I identified the target host and detected an HTTP service running on port 80.

## Burp Suite

- I configured Burp Suite as an intercepting proxy between the browser and DVWA.

- This helped me understand how HTTP requests and responses travel between a web browser and a web application. I also learned how to inspect request and response headers.

## Wireshark

- I used Wireshark to capture and analyze network traffic between Kali Linux and DVWA.

--> Capture network packets
--> Filter TCP and HTTP traffic
--> Identify source and destination IP addresses
--> Examine protocol information
--> Analyze individual packets
--> Practical Skills Developed

### Through this project, I developed practical knowledge of:

- Virtual machine deployment
- Network configuration
- Network troubleshooting
- Port scanning
- Service enumeration
- HTTP traffic interception
- Packet capture
- Network traffic analysis
- Cybersecurity lab setup

### Key Takeaway

This project helped me connect theoretical cybersecurity concepts with practical tools and techniques. Working with Kali Linux, DVWA, Nmap, Burp Suite, and Wireshark gave me hands-on experience with network reconnaissance, web traffic analysis, and packet inspection in a controlled laboratory environment.

The project also helped me understand the importance of performing security testing in an isolated and authorized environment.
